# Purpose

You are working inside the AI Book Framework repository.

This repository is NOT a novel.

This repository is a reusable framework that helps authors write novels with AI.

Always distinguish between the framework itself and the future book projects that will use it.

---

# Core Concepts

The framework consists of several major subsystems.

- Documentation
- AI Agents
- Project Memory
- Knowledge Base
- Prompt Library
- Templates
- Cursor Rules
- Development Workflow
- Git Integration

Each subsystem has a single responsibility.

Do not mix responsibilities.

---

# Project Layers

Layer 1

Framework

Contains reusable logic, documentation, rules and templates.

Layer 2

Novel Project

Contains one specific novel.

Examples:

book/
chapters/
drafts/

Layer 3

Generated Content

Draft chapters, revisions, exported manuscripts and related assets.

---

# Single Source of Truth

Information should exist in only one place.

Reference existing documents instead of duplicating content.

When new information belongs to an existing document, update that document rather than creating another one.

---

# Repository Philosophy

Prefer a small number of well-structured documents over many overlapping documents.

Every file should have a clear purpose.

Avoid creating "misc", "temp", "notes2", "copy", "final-final" style files.

---

# Documentation Standards

Documentation is part of the product.

Write documentation for humans first.

Use clear headings.

Prefer examples over abstract descriptions.

Keep terminology consistent throughout the repository.

---

# Quality

When creating new files, ensure they fit naturally into the existing repository structure.

If a proposed file duplicates an existing responsibility, improve the existing file instead of creating a new one.

The repository should become easier to understand over time, not more complex.